Requirements:
Admission to the College of Business requires students to be admitted to the university. Specific requirements for admission to the college and its degree programs include:
*   Completion of a minimum of 30 hours of college credit;
*   Minimum overall 2.5 GPA on all college work attempted;
*   Minimum 2.5 GPA in all courses completed at UNT;
*   Completion of the College of Business Foundation Courses (CBAF) with a minimum 2.5 GPA (note that a minimum grade of C is required in each course);
*   Completion of the following courses as part of the CBAF requirements: ENGL 1310, ENGL 1320 (or equivalent); MATH 1350, MATH 1351 (or equivalent); ECON 1100, ECON 1110 (or equivalent); BCIS 2610; DSCI 2710; ACCT 2010, ACCT 2020; BLAW 3430; FINA 3770; MGMT 3720; MKTG 3650.
*   Students must complete the College of Business Foundation courses prior to enrolling in 3000/4000-level professional courses.
